  "allowed_effect": "Only parent --execute may replace the exact local routes-reelles.json registry after validation/backups; no other route or process is changed.",
  "checks": [
    {
      "lines": "79-122,224-270",
      "finding": "Only roots absent->allocated_pending->worker_ready is proposed. Same source/plan/Luna/MAX/reserved session, actual distinct job and pinned marker are bound. Duplicate/skip/rollback/replay and changed job/allocation/submission/observed worker bindings or terminal receipt refuse. Observed route removal refuses. Non-roots routes and registry metadata remain exactly equal; active dynamic lanes remain <=3 alongside SO."
    },
    {
      "lines": "231-239",
      "finding": "The input registry is read under its current raw SHA. observer_state must be an immutable received snapshot rather than the known live observer-state path. History is used for monotonic validation and never written. The parent remains responsible for snapshot provenance and actual freshness."
    },
    {
      "lines": "178-221",
      "finding": "Ready transition binds the actual local authorization, exact source/plan/integration-review/Q artifacts, request digest, cache path, CELL-BINDING equality and worker-ready PID/model/MAX/session/auth/CLI. Two complete related identities, same command and distinct PIDs are required; metadata UTC normalization preserves seven fractional digits. OWNER is exact five-field protocol/session/model/MAX/job."
    },
    {
      "lines": "125-175",
      "finding": "Windows quoting is parsed by CommandLineToArgvW without executing the command. The exact sealed bootstrap, roots/job/session/cache, authorization/config/OWNER paths and their hashes, permitted mailbox namespace, unique exact flags and one execute switch are checked; extra or duplicate flags refuse."
    },
    {
      "lines": "273-313",
      "finding": "Publication revalidates the input/proposal and every direct artifact ref; exclusively named original-route/history backups are preserved byte-identically. The original-route backup and same-directory proposed tempfile are flushed/fsynced, a linked exclusive intent is written, and unchanged original bytes are checked immediately before os.replace. Published bytes are reread and a separate observed receipt is written. A concurrent original change refuses without overwrite."
    },
    {
      "lines": "316-336",
      "finding": "Default is dry-run with no output mutation. The CLI entrypoint admits only the exact resolved observer registry target; explicit execute and a local exclusive parent lock are required for publication. No process, census, CLI, remote transport, RPC, worker, model or factory action exists. Publication receipts stay verified:false and native_generation_admitted:false."
    }
  ],
  "validation_evidence": {
    "sealed_manifest_files_rehashed_and_sized": 14,
    "preserved_author_synthetic_tests_passed": 12,
    "preserved_author_ruff_passed": true,
    "reviewer_read_tests_and_logs": true,
    "reviewer_reran_tests": false,
    "reason_not_rerun": "No new unresolved concrete defect justified another run. Tests cover unchanged foreign routes/metadata/history, altered refs/job/session/effort, repeat/skip/rollback/immutable replacement, duplicate jobs, identity metadata, synthetic ready argv and atomic replacement/concurrent change in temporary directories."
  },
  "operator_conditions": [
    "The parent must supply the real immutable observer-state copy, actual submitted job/marker and later actual cache/ready/CELL-BINDING/OWNER/relay identity copies. Metadata linkage alone does not prove live process presence.",
    "After pending publication, wait for the passive reader to observe the corresponding history and obtain the actual reader admission. After bootstrap and ready, publish worker_ready, then perform the real complete-CIM/pair/observer preflight before uploading readyLAST.",
    "The helper is not the freshness, allocation-resource or full native authorization validator. The sealed factory/runtime/observer checks and unchanged original600-second request deadline remain mandatory.",
    "On any failure during or after atomic replacement, preserve backup/intent/temp/current route and reconcile the actual file hash before another operation. Do not treat an exception as proof that publication had no effect; no automatic replay or rollback is admitted."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "An exclusive snapshot path and hashes do not independently authenticate the producer or establish current process/CIM actuality. Those remain the parent's real observations.",
    "The local lock serializes this helper; it is not a filesystem-wide compare-and-swap or a hardware durability guarantee. The code checks for concurrent registry changes and uses atomic replacement, but cannot exclude an unrelated writer racing after the last check.",
    "Historical snapshot and intent backup writes are exclusive; only the original-route backup and proposed tempfile explicitly fsync. The review does not claim every artifact or directory metadata is power-loss durable.",
    "No generation permission, model call, first NORMAL/evaluation, pilot, scientific gain, process shutdown or global admission is produced by this helper or review."
  ],
